{"folioDeck": 1, "exportedAt": "2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z", "meta": {"id": "amabc", "title": "Amharic Alphabet (Fidäl)", "subtitle": "44 orders, letters and signs · both directions, as two cards each", "desc": "The Ethiopic script (fidäl) in which Amharic is written: 44 notes. The first deck of the Amharic collection. Fidäl is an abugida: every character is a consonant with one of seven vowels, the ORDERS, and each order is a regular mark on the consonant's shape — so the deck teaches the seven orders first (ቡ ሉ ሙ: a stroke on the right is u), then the 34 consonants in the traditional order (ሀ ለ ሐ መ …), each with its whole row of seven, then the labialised -wa forms (ሏ ቧ) and the rounded kʷ gʷ ḳʷ, and the punctuation. Both directions: see a letter and recall its sound, or see a sound and recall the letter, each a card with its own schedule. Every note gives the romanisation the level decks use (English Wiktionary's), the sound described in English words and, for a consonant, the commonest word that begins with it. The sounds are approximations, as every learner's alphabet gives them; where English has no equivalent — the ejectives ḳ ṭ č̣ p̣ ṣ, said with the throat closed and released in a pop — the card says what to do instead. Amharic says several letters alike (ሀ ሐ ኀ are all h; ሰ ሠ; አ ዐ; ጸ ፀ), and words are spelt with either; the romanisation keeps them apart (h ḥ ḫ, s ś, ʾ ʿ, ṣ ṣ́) and so does this deck. There is no speaker button: few devices have an Amharic voice. Sources: the standard description of modern Amharic (Wikipedia, 'Amharic' and 'Ge'ez script'); the romanisation is English Wiktionary's (Module:Ethi-translit), and the example words, their romanisations and meanings are English Wiktionary's, via the kaikki.org extraction (CC BY-SA 4.0), chosen by their frequency in the Amharic Wikipedia.", "author": "", "language": "en", "color": "#85063D", "tags": ["amharic", "alphabet", "fidel", "ethiopic"], "glossMode": "site", "types": {"am-abc": {"id": "am-abc", "name": "Amharic letter", "speechLang": "am-ET", "fields": ["Letter", "Row", "Sound", "Example"], "cards": [{"name": "Letter → sound", "front": "<div class=\"uc-letter\">{{Letter}}</div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-row\">{{Row}}</div><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div>{{#Example}}<div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}</div>{{/Example}}</div>"}, {"name": "Sound → letter", "front": "<div class=\"uc-ask\">Which letter is this?</div><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div></div>", "back": "{{FrontSide}}<hr><div class=\"uc-letter\">{{Letter}}</div><div class=\"uc-row\">{{Row}}</div><div class=\"uc-field\"><div class=\"uc-pos\">sound</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Sound}}</div>{{#Example}}<div class=\"uc-pos uc-gap\">as in</div><div class=\"uc-gl\">{{Example}}</div>{{/Example}}</div>"}], "css": ".card {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 17px;\n  line-height: 1.6;\n}\n.uc-ask {\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  opacity: 0.55;\n}\n.uc-letter {\n  font-size: 60px;\n  font-weight: 400;\n  line-height: 1.3;\n}\n.uc-say {\n  margin-left: 14px;\n  vertical-align: middle;\n  font-size: 15px;\n}\n.uc-field {\n  display: block;\n  width: fit-content;\n  min-width: min(300px, 100%);\n  max-width: 100%;\n  margin: 14px auto 0;\n  padding: 11px 15px;\n  border: 1px solid var(--rule, rgba(0,0,0,0.12));\n  border-radius: 11px;\n  text-align: left;\n  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper-2, #EFEDE6) 58%, var(--card, #FFFFFF));\n}\n.uc-pos {\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n  font-size: 9.5px;\n  letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--ink-faint, #6C6A63);\n}\n.uc-gap {\n  margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.uc-gl {\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.uc-rm {\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.uc-ex {\n  font-size: 21px;\n}\n.uc-exr {\n  margin-left: 6px;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n.uc-exe {\n  margin-left: 6px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n.uc-row {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 6px 14px;\n  margin-top: 6px;\n}\n.uc-ri {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  min-width: 38px;\n}\n.uc-rc {\n  font-size: 30px;\n  line-height: 1.25;\n}\n.uc-rr {\n  font-size: 13px;\n  opacity: 0.62;\n}\n"}}, "version": 1, "createdAt": "2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z", "forkedFrom": null}, "cards": [{"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ለ በ መ", "Row": "<span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ለ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">lä</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">በ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">bä</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">መ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">mä</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሰ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">sä</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ነ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">nä</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ከ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">kä</span></span>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">ä</span> · the first order, like the u of cup or the a of about, short; after h and the glottal stop (ሀ, አ) it is said a. The mark: the bare shape, with no mark: ለ በ መ", "Example": ""}, "id": "u_amabc_1", "type": "am-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ሉ ቡ ሙ", "Row": "<span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሉ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">lu</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ቡ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">bu</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሙ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">mu</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሱ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">su</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ኑ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">nu</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ኩ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ku</span></span>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">u</span> · the second order, &quot;oo&quot; as in food. The mark: a short stroke on the right side, halfway down: ሉ ቡ ሙ", "Example": ""}, "id": "u_amabc_2", "type": "am-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ሊ ቢ ሚ", "Row": "<span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሊ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">li</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ቢ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">bi</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሚ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">mi</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሲ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">si</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ኒ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ni</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ኪ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ki</span></span>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">i</span> · the third order, &quot;ee&quot; as in see. The mark: a short stroke at the foot of the right leg: ሊ ቢ ሚ", "Example": ""}, "id": "u_amabc_3", "type": "am-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ላ ባ ማ", "Row": "<span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ላ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">la</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ባ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ba</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ማ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ma</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሳ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">sa</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ና</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">na</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ካ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">ka</span></span>", "Sound": "<span class=\"uc-rm\">a</span> · the fourth order, &quot;a&quot; as in father. The mark: the right leg lengthened, or a short leg added: ላ ባ ማ", "Example": ""}, "id": "u_amabc_4", "type": "am-abc"}, {"sub": "", "fields": {"Letter": "ሌ ቤ ሜ", "Row": "<span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ሌ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">le</span></span><span class=\"uc-ri\"><span class=\"uc-rc\">ቤ</span><span class=\"uc-rr\">be</span></span><span c